[{:adr/id "2607124600"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-5820 gains a minimal HTTP service layer (first step toward live operation)"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/related ["2607121900-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-crm-coverage" "2607122400-cloud-itonami-crm-fleet-dashboard-analytics"]
  :adr/loop-context "First cycle of a /loop dynamic-mode self-paced task ('raise maturity toward live production operation') launched after the owner asked for a 5-stage maturity assessment and was told the fleet sits at the top of stage 2 / entry of stage 3 (MVP) -- no UI/service surface, no real LLM wiring, no persistent store, no deployment."
  :adr/decision "Added src/crm/http.clj (JVM-only compat layer, correct per CLAUDE.md's runtime-priority rules since no portable HTTP-server primitive exists at the kotoba-wasm/clojurewasm/cljs/nbb level): GET / (no auth, info), GET /health (no auth, store reachability), POST /propose (bearer auth, thin adapter over the EXISTING crm.operation StateGraph, no governance logic reimplemented), GET /dashboard (bearer auth, routes through the EXISTING crm.policy/check :pipeline/dashboard-query RBAC rule unchanged, never bypassed)."
  :adr/auth-design "Bearer token from $ISIC5820_API_TOKEN, fail-closed both ways: start-server! throws on blank/nil token; -main exits 1 without ever starting the listener if the env var is unset. No default/hardcoded token, no auth-disabled fallback path."
  :adr/escalation-handling "An :escalate (human-in-the-loop) graph result is surfaced honestly as HTTP 202 with thread-id and reason, not hidden or silently blocked -- an approval/rejection submission endpoint is explicitly out of scope for this first layer, documented in docs/api.md."
  :adr/dependencies-added "http-kit 2.8.1, ring/ring-core 1.15.3, org.clojure/data.json 2.5.2 -- all confirmed resolving; new :serve alias added to deps.edn"
  :adr/honest-scope "docs/api.md explicitly states: single-process, single-tenant, no TLS termination, no rate limiting, and critically that -main runs against crm.store/seed-db (the same demo dataset crm.sim uses) so process restarts lose all state -- real persistent-store wiring is left as a follow-up, not silently glossed over"
  :adr/test-status "45 tests / 158 assertions (up from 37/137 pre-existing), 0 failures, lint 0 errors/0 warnings. Tests start a real http-kit server on an ephemeral port and drive it with real HTTP requests (java.net.http), covering unauthenticated health, 401 without token, committed/held decisions via /propose, and RBAC 403/200 on /dashboard."
  :adr/known-gap "Bearer-token comparison uses plain string equality (=), not a constant-time comparison -- a theoretical timing-attack surface not yet mitigated or documented in docs/api.md; flagged here as a follow-up item for a future cycle."
  :adr/remaining-gaps-to-production "No real LLM wired in (advisor remains sealed/sim), no persistent store backing (-main uses ephemeral seed-db), no TLS/reverse-proxy/observability/rate-limiting, no actual deployment, cloud-itonami-isic-6201/6202 do not yet have an equivalent HTTP layer"
  :adr/test-status-commit "c776fdfa2..., pushed to github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820"
  :adr/scope-note "New ADR, not an addendum, because this is a cross-cutting infrastructure capability (network service surface) rather than a domain/business-logic change to the actor's governed pipeline"}]
